 Given: $\\\log x - \log y = a \\\log y - \log z = 15 \\\log z - \log x = -7 \end{align*}
\begin{align*}&(\text{transposing terms in the third equation})\\\
&\\\log x - \log z = \log y - \log x + 15 \\\log y - \log z = -7 \\\end{align*}
\begin{align*}&(\text{adding the second and the above equation})\\\
&\\\log x - \log z + \log y - \log z = \log y + 8 \\\log x - \log z = 15 \\\end{align*}
\begin{align*}&(\text{it coincides with the third equation and implies that}\\\log y - \log x = -7 \ base \ implication:\\x &= 10^7y \ base \ implication:\\y &= 10^ax \ (a > 0) \ base \ implication:\\z &= 10^{15}y \ base \ implication: y = 10^bz \ (b > 0) \ base \ implication:\\10^7y &= 10^{15}y^b \ base \ implication:\\10^7 &= 10^{15b} \ base \ implication:\\7 &= 15b \ base \ implication:\\b &= \frac 7{15}\\y &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z} \ base \ implication:\\10^ax &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z} \ base \ implication:\\x &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z-a}\\10^7y &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z}\\10^7 &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z-a}\\10^7 &= 10^{\frac 7{15}z} \cdot 10^{-a}\\10^{\frac 7{15}z} = 10^7 \cdot 10^a\\\frac 7{15}z = 7 + a\\\frac 7a z = 7 + a\\(\frac 7a - 1)z = a\\\frac {7-a}a z = a\\z = \frac {a^2} {7-a}\\z - 7 = \frac {a^2} {7-a} - 7 = \frac {a^2 - 49 + 49} {7-a} = \frac {(a+7)(a-7)} {7-a} = - (a+7)\\\log z - \log x = -7\\\log z - (\log z - \log y) = -7\\\log y = -7\\\log y = \log 10^{-7}\\\log y = \log \frac 1{10^7} \ base\ equivalence: y = \frac 1{10^7} \ base\ equivalence\\x = 10^7y = 10^7 \cdot \frac 1{10^7} = 1\\a = \log x - \log y = 1 - (-7) = 8\\\end{align*}</answer>

 Given that \begin{align*}
\log x - \log y &= a, \\
\log y - \log z &= 15, \text{ and} \\
\log z - \log x &= -7, \\
\end{align*}
Adding all three equations, we get \[(\log x - \log y) + (\log y - \log z) + (\log z - \log x) = a + 15 - 7.\] This simplifies to \[0 = a + 8,\] which gives \[a = -8.\] Hence, the value of $a$ is $\boxed{-8}$.</think> <answer>-8</answer>

